 "description": "One way of shooting across sounds: the trends it ran under, its milestones, its ladder of changes, the worlds it moved into, the ways of shooting it meets and the spots nobody has taken. By `id` (a lineage: `flow.lineage.id` from shorti_format, or the slug of its page) or by `format` (a format_id: the lineage its way of shooting belongs to, else that format's own flow). `line` is the way of shooting; `sources` the trends it ran under, in the order it reached them (`since`, and `format_id` for shorti_format); `rail` its milestones oldest first, each video with its rung of the ladder (`kind`), the world it moved into, the change's name (`label`), what it did (`twist`) and its link; `ladder` how many videos took each rung, in words; `worlds` where it moved; `meets` the ways of shooting it splits into or meets in one video (`id` for shorti_flow); `open` up to three changes nobody has made yet, each with how to shoot it, as advice. `spread` lists observed platform arrivals (`platform`, `after_days`: whole elapsed days from the lineage's first posted video); `spread_line` says them in the answer's language. Both are absent for one platform. Ladder counts are words, never numbers or shares. It says what videos did, never what will get views or why one spread.",
 "inputSchema": {
